@@ -102,7 +102,9 @@ ### Ticket
 
 **Immutability enforcement:** the write-once rule is enforced on the `Ticket` model (`updating` hook), so it applies to Eloquent saves only — mass updates through the query builder (`Ticket::query()->update(...)`) bypass it and must not be used on issued tickets.
 
-**Single-ticket call (scope note):** `Ticket::call()` marks one waiting ticket as `called` (exactly-once). Deterministic call-next selection (priority + age + 3-ticket fairness) is implemented by `App\Actions\CallNextTicket` with the three call-panel modes below (`any` applies fairness; `priority_only`/`normal_only` ignore it). Both call paths enforce the **same effective queue authorization rule** (`QueuePolicy::call`): owner/admin bypass without a grant row, employees require a `queue_access.call` grant for that queue, non-members are denied with no ticket mutation. HTTP/Livewire panels remain future work.
+**Single-ticket call (scope note):** `Ticket::call()` marks one waiting ticket as `called` (exactly-once). Deterministic call-next selection (priority + age + 3-ticket fairness) is implemented by `App\Actions\CallNextTicket` with the three call-panel modes below (`any` applies fairness; `priority_only`/`normal_only` ignore it). Both call paths enforce the **same effective queue authorization rule** (`QueuePolicy::call`): owner/admin bypass without a grant row, employees require a `queue_access.call` grant for that queue, non-members are denied with no ticket mutation.
+
+**Queue UI (Livewire):** managers use `entity.queues` (`App\Livewire\Entity\Queues`) to create, rename, (de)activate and grant call access; the page calls the domain actions and surfaces their validation errors instead of duplicating rules. Any member with a callable queue uses `entity.serve` (`App\Livewire\Entity\Serve`) to see the waiting list (same ordering/mode filters as `CallNextTicket`, first 30) and call the next ticket. Every client-supplied queue/membership id is re-resolved scoped to the current entity (`$entity->queues()->findOrFail()`, `$entity->memberships()->findOrFail()`), so foreign ids fail without disclosing or changing anything. Successful calls are rate-limited per user and entity.
 
